module gunbc.tools.self_host_closure_terminal_causes

import v2.std.algebra { any, filter, length }
import v2.std.collection { List }
import v2.std.integer { Int }
import v2.std.logic { Bool }
import v2.std.node { Symbol }
import v2.std.text { String }

// THE TERMINAL-CAUSE TABLE FOR THE V2 SELF-HOST CLOSURE, from the native driver's own per-file
// output. The subject is the INPUT CLOSURE of src/v2/compiler/00_compile.dag - the modules the
// emitted-native compiler is actually built from - and not the directory census a reader counting
// *.dag under src/v2/compiler would reach. The closure is a fact about imports, it is carried below
// as closure_module_manifest, and its width is length over that roster. How much of it the emitted
// compiler's own front end refuses is length over closure_refusal_rows.
//
// WHY THE TERMINAL DIAGNOSTIC AND NOT THE HEAD. A rejection is a LIST, and rejected_with_pending
// prepends the grammar-global overlap residue to every parse failure, so the head reason is the
// same symbol on almost every row and discriminates nothing. The row therefore carries the LAST
// diagnostic - the cause that actually refused - at the same fatal grain
// v2.workflow.compile_door_ledger owns its FatalGrain rows at. The cause symbols here are those
// symbols; nothing is re-coined.
//
// WHY A CAUSE ROSTER SEPARATE FROM THE FILE ROWS. One defect surfaces under several stop lexemes
// and in several files, and one file can carry several defects, so file and cause are two
// populations joined by a relation - not one row each. The displayed stop lexeme is where the
// parser gave up, never the cause: it is the NEXT declaration's leading keyword as often as it is
// the offending token.
//
// ARE THE CAUSES SHARED ACROSS FILES? Yes, and that is the load-bearing result. The concentration is
// at both ends, and cause_population is what says how far: a module body that reaches no function
// declaration and a raw newline inside a string literal are the two largest slices between them, and
// the parse class is the mirror image - a single terminal reason standing for the most causes of any,
// which is why its file count was never its work size. Ask cause_population for a defect's reach and
// rows_for_cause for its subjects; no count is written here, because the rows beside this note
// already determine every one of them and a numeral copied out of them rots the moment a lane
// repairs a row. Sharing runs the other way too - one file can carry several defects, so the
// per-cause populations overlap and do not sum to the row count - and it crosses stop lexemes: the
// same defect is reported at `fn`, at `data`, at `type` and at its own token depending only on where
// the parser happened to give up.
//
// HOW THIS TABLE IS RE-DERIVED, AND WHERE THE PRODUCER RESOLVES - which is NOT this base, and saying
// otherwise would be the unreachable citation this module refuses to make elsewhere.
//
// The population and the terminal causes come from the emitted native compiler's own per-file output,
// reached by `claim_executor --required-ci --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --required-lane
// v2-native`, whose context fold emits one NativeTestFileRefusal row per source carrying the head and
// fatal reason. That lane, its authority gunbc.witness_v2_native_route, and the NativeTestFileRefusal
// row type all resolve AT THE PINNED HEAD BELOW and at no commit on this branch's base: they are
// #10882's, unmerged at this writing. The pin's head_sha is therefore not decoration - it is the only
// tree in which this citation resolves, and a reader who checks it out gets the producer.
//
// The per-declaration reduction behind each cause comes from a probe that calls
// v2.compiler.program_assembly program_assembly_read_to_normalized_root_prepared - the same per-file
// path that fold takes, so every stage the fold can refuse at is reachable from it. That symbol does
// resolve here.
//
// WHAT A READER MAY NOT DO WITH IT. There is no aggregate verdict, because the population IS the
// finding; a Boolean over it would be a verdict on subjects that have not each been separately
// established. Each cause carries how its per-file join was backed, and the two backings are not
// the same rung - see JoinEvidence.

// THIS CARRIER'S STANDING: A HAND-AUTHORED, REVISION-SCOPED SNAPSHOT. It is stated here because the
// table is not one kind of thing, and only half of it is a projection.
//
// The PROJECTED half is the population and the terminal causes. The v2-native lane's context fold
// already emits exactly one {path, head_reason, fatal_reason} row per source - at the pinned head, not
// on this base - and closure_module_manifest is likewise derivable from the emitted crate's per-module
// headers. Those rows are hand-applied here, which is the manual-application-committed-as-source tell,
// and they are the part that should stop being authored.
// dissolve-on: an emission target for this table plus a drift gate over it, in the shape
// gunbc.generated_artifact_gate already carries - at which point the projected rows are generated and
// the hand-authored copy is deleted, not migrated.
//
// The AUTHORED half is the cause roster and the per-file attribution: eighteen defects, each with a
// reproducer, a positive control, a nearest-alternative control and its join evidence. No producer in
// this repository emits those, because they are the output of reduction - prefix isolation, a ladder
// of single edits, and delta-debugging - and not of a fold. Generating this table today would
// therefore cover the projected half and fork the authored half away from it, which is a worse state
// than one carrier that says which half is which.
// dissolve-on: reduction becomes a modeled fold whose result the lane can emit; until that capability
// exists this half has no producer to name, and saying otherwise would be naming an instrument that
// does not exist.

// WHO CONSUMES THIS TABLE, AND BY WHAT ROUTE. Stated as one of DESIGN 3c's three honest states rather
// than left for a reader to infer: this is the SECOND state - a declared frontier with its trigger
// beside it - and not the first.
//
// TODAY: nothing outside this module's own witness reads these rows by execution. The witness asserts
// properties OF THE TABLE, which is a real check of this artifact but is not an executing consumer of
// the measurement, and the repair lanes that cite causes by key do so as readers, which is citation
// and not a route.
//
// THE NAMED CONSUMER AND ITS TRIGGER: v2.workflow.compile_door_ledger cause_ownership_lookup, joined
// at FATAL grain against every terminal_reason carried below. That join is not authorable on this
// base: known_frontier_causes here carries four causes and all four are HEAD-grain, none of the five
// terminal reasons this table reports among them, so a witness asserting the join would be red today
// and would green on the repair - the wrong direction for every subject involved. The grain-keyed
// lookup and the fatal-grain ownership rows for exactly these five causes land with #10882; when that
// is on main, the join becomes an executing route with an authorable red - a row naming a cause the
// ledger does not own at fatal grain turns it false - and this frontier closes.

// THE PIN. Every row is an observation of ONE tree through ONE binary. The emitted closure's own
// reported identity is byte-derived and therefore unstable across emissions (the seed emitter emits
// its re-export lines in unordered-set order), so an ORDER-INSENSITIVE digest is carried beside it
// as the key two runs can join on. The driver binary digest is the strongest of the three:
// rebuilding it from a SECOND emission of the same sources produced identical bytes, which is what
// establishes that the re-export delta is inert rather than merely believed to be.
//
// THE GRAMMAR-PREPARE RESIDUE IS PINNED HERE because the repair lanes need a BEFORE number and a
// number that lives in a message is unreachable from the thing that owns it. It is prepare_grammar's
// own non-fatal residue at this head - the advisory rejected_with_pending prepends to every parse
// failure, which is why the head grain discriminates nothing. It is a property of the GRAMMAR and not
// of the corpus, so a lane adding a production can move it in either direction and a rise is not by
// itself a regression: a production that overlaps an existing choice adds residue rows even when it
// parses everything it was added for.
//
// WHAT THE PIN DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CARRY is a digest of the per-declaration reduction probe. That
// probe is a recipe in docs/plans/self-host-closure-terminal-causes.md, not an artifact in this tree,
// so a digest of it would pin an identity no reader here can reproduce - an unreachable citation,
// which is worse than none. The route that IS executable from this repository is the one that
// produced the population and the terminal causes, and it is named below.
type ObservationPin {
  head_sha: String
  emitted_closure_identity_as_reported: String
  order_insensitive_closure_digest: String
  emitted_driver_binary_digest: String
  compiler_source_manifest_digest: String
  grammar_prepare_residue_total: Int
}

// HOW A CAUSE WAS JOINED TO THE FILES IT EXPLAINS. The three arms are different rungs and the
// distinction is the point: an executed join re-ran the compiler over a modified subject and
// watched the refusal go away, a signature join matched the construct in the isolated culprit
// declaration and did not. Every cause's RULE is executed either way; this field is about the
// per-file attribution only, and calling a signature match executed would be the inflation the
// guarantee ladder forbids.
type JoinEvidence
  = JoinedByExecutedNeutralizer
  | JoinedByExecutedClosureIdentityJoin
  | JoinedBySignatureOverIsolatedDeclaration

// ONE DEFECT. key is the short id the repair lanes cite; id names the defect; terminal_reason is
// the symbol the driver reported. The three text fields are PROGRAM TEXT, not commentary: the input
// that refuses, the input that accepts, and the control that separates this cause from its nearest
// alternative. A line break inside them is written as an escape, because a raw newline inside a
// string literal is itself one of the causes rostered below.
// WHAT THE NEAREST-ALTERNATIVE CONTROL ESTABLISHED. Both arms exclude an alternative and they exclude
// different ones: a control that ACCEPTS shows the neighbouring construct is innocent, so the cause is
// not the wider class it sits in; a control that REFUSES IDENTICALLY shows the cause does not depend on
// the detail that control varied.
//
// THE VERDICT IS THE CONSTRUCTOR, NOT A FIELD BESIDE THE INPUT. An earlier revision carried the control
// text and its verdict as two fields, which left the verdict readable by a human and consumed by
// nothing - and the only carrier-decidable check over it turned out to be implied by the
// copied-control wall, so adding one would have been the redundant witness this file has already
// deleted twice. As a variant the question cannot be dodged: reading the input at all eliminates the
// arm, so every consumer of the control has consumed the verdict, by construction rather than by a
// check that re-states it.
type NearestAlternativeControl
  = ControlThatAccepts { input: String }
  | ControlThatRefusesIdentically { input: String }

type FrontEndCause {
  key: Symbol
  id: Symbol
  terminal_reason: Symbol
  rejecting_reproducer: String
  positive_control: String
  discriminating_control: NearestAlternativeControl
  join_evidence: JoinEvidence
}

// THE CLOSURE ITSELF, as the denominator every row is a fraction of. It is derived, not listed by
// hand: the emitted probe crate writes one Rust file per closure module carrying a `// Source
// module:` header, and joining those headers against each `.dag` file's own `module` line yields
// exactly these paths. It is carried because a population without its denominator invites the
// directory census this table exists to replace - and because it is the only thing a refusal row's
// path can be joined AGAINST, which is what makes the membership witness a real check rather than a
// comparison of two numerals authored side by side.
